# ============================================================
# ITM Server Security Monitor
# Web scan exclusions
#
# Installed to /etc/security-monitor/ioc/web-exclusions.conf
#
# Shell globs matched against the FULL PATH. A matching file is
# never reported by any web content module.
#
# Use this for confirmed false positives only, and write down
# why. Every entry here is a hole in the detection: a webshell
# dropped at an excluded path will not be reported.
#
# Prefer the narrowest possible glob. Exclude a file, not a
# directory tree, wherever you can.
# ============================================================

# --- example: a legitimate database tool, confirmed by hash ---
# /website/tools/adminer.php

# --- example: an editorial article that legitimately discusses
#     online gambling regulation ---
# /website/deputi1/berita/2026/regulasi-judi-online.html

# --- example: a vendor library that uses eval() by design ---
# /website/*/vendor/twig/twig/src/Environment.php

# --- framework caches that are regenerated constantly and are
#     already excluded by WEB_EXCLUDE_DIRS; listed here as a
#     reminder of the safe pattern ---
# /website/*/storage/framework/views/*.php
